Subject: Force fixed Reactor Netty and Reactor Core versions for CVE-2025-22227
Description: Pin the compatible fixed Reactor release train so runtime dependency resolution cannot select vulnerable Reactor Netty artifacts.
Origin: DHI-internal (Nessie CVE remediation)
CVE: CVE-2025-22227
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/projectnessie/nessie 6af26e74f89cf99624328aed2148b1619fa4ce20 servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
Adaptation: Rebased the force block after publishingHelper and before the existing Netty force block in Nessie 0.110.0.
Regenerate: `git apply jackson-core-2.22.3.patch netty-4.2.17.patch`, then insert the Reactor resolution strategy after publishingHelper.
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI Gradle force overlay)
Drop-When: dependency io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http >= 1.2.18
Verify: sbom pkg:maven/io.projectreactor.netty/reactor-netty-http@1.2.18

---
diff --git a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
--- a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
@@ -32,6 +32,20 @@

 publishingHelper { mavenName = "Nessie - Quarkus Server" }

+// Force reactor-netty to 1.2.18 to resolve CVE-2025-22227 (only fixed in reactor-netty
+// >= 1.2.8). reactor-netty 1.2.x belongs to the Reactor 2024.0 train and requires
+// reactor-core 3.7.x, so reactor-core is pinned to 3.7.19 to keep the train
+// consistent.
+configurations.configureEach {
+  resolutionStrategy {
+    force(
+      "io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-http:1.2.18",
+      "io.projectreactor.netty:reactor-netty-core:1.2.18",
+      "io.projectreactor:reactor-core:3.7.19",
+    )
+  }
+}
+
 // Quarkus platform constraints and Nessie's declared Netty version still allow dependency
 // resolution to select older, vulnerable Netty releases. Force every Netty artifact to a
 // fixed version so the Quarkus fast-jar packaging includes the correct jar filenames and
